The '''thread of Elidinis''' is an uncommon reward from the [[Chest (Tombs of Amascut)|rewards chest]] within the [[Tombs of Amascut]]. Players with 75 [[Crafting]]{{Boostable|yes}} can use the thread on a [[rune pouch]] with a [[needle]] in their [[inventory]] to create a [[divine rune pouch]], which can store four types of [[runes]] instead of three. This process can be reversed to return both items.

The base rate of receiving the thread is 1/10. To [[Bad luck mitigation|mitigate bad luck]], the rate is scaled linearly with the number of raid completions, up to a maximum of 3/10 upon completing 15 raids.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1658043649047887873|date=15 May 2023|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/109799|archivedate=5 August 2023|quote=[(...) The bad luck protection for jewels. Does it cap out at 90 or 270 raids? I.E. 60x1,5 or 180×1,5. (...)] I think it's 1.5 x 180 like you said, so 270 - if I'm reading my colleagues' code directly. (...)}} Once the player gets their first thread, the drop rate is decreased to 1/50.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1654554310867386368|date=5 May 2023|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/108953|archivedate=5 May 2023|quote=[Can you confirm the drop rate of the Thread of elidinis after getting the first one? Is it 1/10? I haven't seen a single duplicate thread for almost 200 raids after losing it.] No, if I'm reading the loot code correctly (which isn't a sure thing, as it isn't something I ever worked on myself) it changes to 1/50 after you've had one of those.}}{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1650416621444276226|date=24 April 2023|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/107850|archivedate=6 May 2023|quote=I'd wonder if that 1/10 advertisement was massively over-simplified. It looks to me like it's affected by whether you already have the jewels, as well as whether you already had a thread (moving the chance to 1/50 as you say).}} Additionally, players can buy the thread from [[Perdu]] for 350,000 [[coins]] if they have obtained it from the Tombs of Amascut at least once.

'''Note:''' This item is destroyed on death.

